{
  "version": 212,
  "released": "2026-08-25",
  "changelog": "v212: the landmark RECORDER \u2014 recording is not replying (ADR 0028, fixes lifehug#221). WHY: on the v207+ platform leaf, two live landmark sessions came back with a warm, engaged reply and `landmark: null`. Asked about military service the person said \"I have not served in the military\" and then told a two-year mission story \u2014 the reply took up the mission and filed nothing, where the domain's own answer was a plain {\"domain\": \"military\", \"none\": true}. Asked about losses they named the people they had lost; the reply named them back and filed nothing. The certification audit (platform #586) executed the chain and returned the decisive fact: the emission instruction had been in that leaf since v203 and was live when the founder answered. Prompt prose alone is not certifiable, and the re-harvest \u2014 which re-composes the identical prompt and one-shots it \u2014 could not heal it either. One completion was doing two jobs and recording lost. FIX: recording is now its own pass. system/landmark_recorder.py + interactions/landmarks/prompt/recorder.md + composition.recorder / role.recorder: the conversation writes the reply, then the RECORDER reads the person's own message and files the record. It carries no identity, no behavior, no examples and no transcript \u2014 only the domain, its ladder, whether the domain can be answered \"never happened\", what is known, the question asked, what they said, and what they were told back \u2014 and emits one object: {\"landmark\": {...}} or {\"landmark\": null}. parse_recorder_output runs BOTH pinned validation layers (conversation_delivery._parse_landmark then validate_landmark), so there is no second vocabulary for what a landmark is. ONE RECORDER, TWO TRIGGERS: record_answer(...) is what a live landmark turn calls after its reply, and what a historical sweep calls over answers people already gave \u2014 the sweep inherits the backstop instead of re-rolling the same dice. THE BACKSTOP: landmark_gates.answer_must_record, the lane's ONE blocking lint, from the single definition landmarks_interaction.answer_must_record; on a finding the recorder regenerates ONCE with recording_reminder(domain) appended (MAX_ATTEMPTS = 2) and then emits, or returns STATUS_WITHHELD carrying the lint id \u2014 never a silent drop, never a fabricated record. Detection is deliberately narrow via one new definition, landmarks_interaction.answer_shape(): a SKIP wins outright (every \"I don't remember\" hedge is swept in there so ambiguity fails toward skip); a NEGATIVE counts only where the domain can carry a none terminal, so \"no siblings\" never lints `family`; SUBSTANTIVE is the model's own acknowledgment shape \u2014 the reply echoing a proper noun or a year the person supplied in that same message, minus anything already in LANDMARKS. An answer with neither name nor year is invisible on purpose: the class blocks, so a false positive would punish a good turn. Because the recorder never needed the reply, a turn whose reply generation FAILED still records. COST, stated honestly in ADR 0028: one extra haiku-class completion per landmark ANSWER \u2014 never on the daily question, never on a session that is not a landmark session \u2014 against a failure that re-asks a question the person already answered. Nothing is removed: the reply keeps its additive `landmark` field and lint_landmark_reply reaches the same single definition, so a host that has not wired the recorder behaves exactly as at v209. The recorder is also told only the keys its domain can READ (landmark_recorder.recordable_keys, derived from the ladder and carried in the leaf) \u2014 the writer-side half of #219/#220's class, where a field validates, stores, and is read by no rung: no `span` offered on `children`, no `label` on `birth`; and the derivation is v211's OWN: recordable_keys walks landmarks_interaction.rung_satisfiers over the ladder, so what the recorder may WRITE and what the ladder can READ are one declaration, bound by a parity test over all nine domains. Prompt work alongside, not instead of: turn-instructions.md and behavior.md now state recording as the turn's first job and name both live cases. TESTS: the landmarks-evals seat gains landmark_gates.answer_must_record at 1.0 compliance and three goldens (the military case and the losses case as the turns they should have been, plus an ambiguous answer that must NOT lint), scored only on turns supplying the person's own message so the gate has a real denominator; landmark-answer-not-recorded-bad-01.json holds both live failures verbatim (surnames synthesized) as the recorder's acceptance, and tests/test_landmarks.py walks lint -> reminder -> emit, the bounded-at-one retry, the withheld terminal, the no-reply case, and the provider-failure case.",
